# handler_callers.allow - rows of mime_handlers[] and names of ej_handlers[] (httpd/web.c) that have no caller
# in the shipped web files or open code, and why each is still there. Read by test_handler_callers.py.
# One line per name:  name <TAB> reason.  The name is the row's pattern exactly as in the table, or the hook name.
# One file for the three source lines: a line naming something a tree does not have is ignored there; a line
# whose name HAS a caller is stale and fails the test, unless its reason carries [not on every line].
# Verdict words: KEEP = stays for the reason given (the ASK lines of batch B were decided on 2026-11-21: removed in batch C or kept);
# NOT-BUILT = inside a build condition no Reaper model sets; FILE-ROW = a file-serving row with no file.
# Proof per name: docs of the v3.8.4 change (proof.tsv, 2026-11-21).
#
# ---- request addresses kept, with their reason
appGet_image_path.cgi	KEEP (low value: the one unused row without sign-in; prints six constant image paths)
backup_all_usericon.cgi	KEEP (client-icon backup / restore; not in an approved batch - the brief names icons as something a node may fetch. Evidence: no cfg_* program names them. Proof clean)
backup_cfg_cntrl.cgi*	KEEP (AiMesh central-control profile backup / restore, RTCONFIG_AMAS_CENTRAL_CONTROL; body in libwebapi; kept with the config-sync rows)
bwm/*.gz	KEEP (owner 2026-11-21: stays. The traffic-history download wo_bwmbackup(); no shipped page names bwm/; read only, but each request can hold the one-connection web server for up to 11 s)
cert.tar	KEEP (brief: keep unless rc's use of the name is explained. Explained: shared/misc.c:543 is a COMMENT - 'cert.crt is archived to /tmp/cert.tar and is used to export certificate' - and no code outside httpd uses the name; the row tars /etc/cert.crt, the public certificate, for a browser download. Proof clean, so it is removable; left in as a read-only export until the owner says so)
change_lang.cgi*	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
change_location.cgi*	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
clean_offline_clientlist.cgi	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
detwan.cgi*	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
get_dev_type_query.cgi	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
get_diag_latest_content_data.cgi	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
get_ipsec_profile.cgi*	KEEP (IPsec read-only exports, not in the approved upload / set list; proof clean)
get_timezone.cgi	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
get_usericon_md5.cgi	KEEP (client-icon backup / restore; not in an approved batch - the brief names icons as something a node may fetch. Evidence: no cfg_* program names them. Proof clean)
ipsec_s2s.conf	KEEP (IPsec read-only exports, not in the approved upload / set list; proof clean)
mDNSNetMonitor.log	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
modemlog.txt*	KEEP (low-value rest, not in an approved batch; proof clean - see KEEP_REVIEW for the ones that act)
save_all_profile.cgi*	KEEP (closed config-sync handler in web_hook.o / libwebapi; the brief keeps these until AiMesh use is ruled out. Evidence so far: cfg_server / cfg_client / libcfgmnt name none of them)
server_ipsec.cert	KEEP (IPsec read-only exports, not in the approved upload / set list; proof clean)
set_TM_EULA.cgi*	KEEP (USED: js/httpApi.js enableEula() builds '/set_' + type + '_EULA.cgi' at run time; js/asus_policy.js calls it with 'tm' from the policy window that GameBoost.asp, AdaptiveQoS_WebHistory.asp and AiProtection_WebProtector.asp open; mobile/pages/boostKey_page.html too - all shipped)
start_config_sync.cgi*	KEEP (closed config-sync handler in web_hook.o / libwebapi; the brief keeps these until AiMesh use is ruled out. Evidence so far: cfg_server / cfg_client / libcfgmnt name none of them)
uploadIconFile.tar	KEEP (client-icon backup / restore; not in an approved batch - the brief names icons as something a node may fetch. Evidence: no cfg_* program names them. Proof clean)
upload_all_usericon.cgi*	KEEP (client-icon backup / restore; not in an approved batch - the brief names icons as something a node may fetch. Evidence: no cfg_* program names them. Proof clean)
upload_blacklist_config.cgi*	KEEP (closed config-sync handler in web_hook.o / libwebapi; the brief keeps these until AiMesh use is ruled out. Evidence so far: cfg_server / cfg_client / libcfgmnt name none of them)
upload_cfg_cntrl.cgi*	KEEP (AiMesh central-control profile backup / restore, RTCONFIG_AMAS_CENTRAL_CONTROL; body in libwebapi; kept with the config-sync rows)
upload_config_sync.cgi*	KEEP (closed config-sync handler in web_hook.o / libwebapi; the brief keeps these until AiMesh use is ruled out. Evidence so far: cfg_server / cfg_client / libcfgmnt name none of them)
